# Persistent logging

# Nothing's camera HAL shim had no label, so it inherited vendor_file and init exec'd it WITHOUT a
# domain transition -- it ran as u:r:init:s0. Every binder call it made was then attributed to init,
# which is where the ~630 "init -> servicemanager/cameraserver : binder" and
# "init -> vendor_file : file : execute{,_no_trans}" denials came from. It is an ordinary camera
# provider, so give it the standard AOSP camera HAL domain.
/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/vendor\.noth\.hardware\.camera-service    u:object_r:hal_camera_default_exec:s0

# HAL/vendor binaries that shipped with NO SELinux label (2026-07-29).
#
# Unlabeled binaries inherit vendor_file, and under ENFORCING init refuses to exec them:
#   "Could not start service 'vendor.power.stats-default' as part of class 'hal': File
#    /vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.power.stats-service (labeled "u:object_r:vendor_file:s0")
#    has incorrect label or no domain transition from u:r:init:s0"
# Under permissive they silently ran as u:r:init:s0, so nothing looked wrong.
#
# power.stats is the one that actually blocked boot: with no IPowerStats, system_server retried
# it as a lazy AIDL service forever and crash-looped (sys.system_server.crash=1), so
# sys.boot_completed was never set. AOSP labels this domain already — it just does not match
# Nothing's binary name (AOSP expects *-service.example / @1.0-service).
/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.power\.stats-service    u:object_r:hal_power_stats_default_exec:s0
